e  to be a mom yeah and i can do it on my  own terms  we are now joined  by wendy mcneill and her beautiful baby  her first live television interview  four months arlo wendy thank you so much  hi friends for joining us and i tell you  you know when i saw you a few months ago  more than a few but  um you told me you know that you were  making this decision and i thought we  should do a story yeah because i've  heard more and more women over the years  making that decision what was the  tipping point for you because you talk  about saying would i be more upset if i  didn't you know have a child but i did  go for trying to get married and whatnot  but what was that tipping point i i had  an aching a longing to be a mother  and for me that meant  doing it by any means necessary and i  had to get realistic about my  circumstances i mean the fact of the  matter is i was in my late 30s  and you know there are certainly  biological pressures that we face  and  you said it was like an article too that  you saw yeah and it felt like i i  basically was  like i had asked the universe i was like  give me a sign that this is the path  that i need to take and the sign the  sign came in the form of this op-ed in  the new york times it was called  um single at 38 have that baby  and i was like  done and i read the one i read the story  and the woman i completely related to  and i was like this is it i'm gonna do  it we know that insurance played a role  in this too i mean you have the coverage  so talk to us about that in terms of you  know women who are watching this or  thinking about that yeah i mean i'm  fortunate that i work for an employer  that you know provides reproductive  insurance and i was able to do this  basically almost nothing out of pocket  little to nothing out of pocket  and that's not you know something that  is extended to a lot of people it's a  blessing they are over making googly  eyes  i gotta get a smile because they got a  smile on me i know she got a smi